-- title:
--   Finite-level approximation of decomposition by Frobenius times inertia
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$, in the sense that the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ belongs to the nonunits of $A$. Let $\varphi$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is a Frobenius element at $A$ for $q$: $\varphi$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and the induced action of $\varphi$ on the residue field of $A$ is $x \mapsto x^{q}$. Let $\sigma$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $L_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be an intermediate field finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$. Then there exist a natural number $n$ and a $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ under the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup into $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, such that $(\varphi^{n}\tau)^{-1}\sigma$ lies in the fixing subgroup of $L_0$, i.e. fixes $L_0$ pointwise. No unramifiedness assumption is imposed, and the exponent $n$ and the inertia element $\tau$ are allowed to depend on $L_0$.
--
--   This is the finite-level form of the classical description of a decomposition group as generated by a Frobenius element together with inertia: every element of the decomposition group at a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $q$ agrees, on any prescribed finite subextension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with a power of a fixed Frobenius times an element of inertia. It is used in the analysis of $q$-adic Galois representations, for instance in establishing ordinarity properties at $q$ and in producing Frobenius-stable lines on inertia-invariant subspaces.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_frobeniusAt_pow_mul_inertia_fixing_of_mem_decompositionSubgroup.lean

